# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Pages' default for static assets is `public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate`,
# which it applies even to content-hashed files. Measured on production: both
# /_astro/_slug_.D0qAjmuO.css and the woff2 fonts came back REVALIDATED with
# that header, so every repeat visit past four hours pays a conditional request
# per asset before it can paint.
#
# Everything below is content-addressed — Astro hashes /_astro/*, and
# scripts/sync.mjs version-stamps the Scalar bundle — so the filename changes
# whenever the bytes do. That is exactly the precondition for `immutable`.
#
# Do NOT extend this to a path whose contents can change under a fixed name;
# a stale immutable response is uncacheable-by-hand and lasts a year.

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/vendor/scalar/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
